PATCH 462: the object-SPAWN core -- b21d returns the NEW slot in DI, b1df registers/zeroes THAT slot, and
every spawn caller splits `mov si,di; pop di` into SI=new object, DI=parent (board:0007 base-loss cascade,
board:0012 self-play).

ASM (re_out/fist_dat_image.bin): b21d (0x1b21d) allocates a roster slot with `mov di,0xa022|0xc05c; add
di,0x37|0xfb ...; mov [di],ax; mov [di+2],bx; clc; ret` -- DI OUT is the new object.  b1df (0x1b1df)
`call b21d; jae; ... mov [si],di; inc [si+2]; mov bx,[di]; ... mov si,di; add si,4; rep zero` registers
and zeroes the NEW slot (ax out = display index), and its callers all do `push di; mov ax,TYPE; lcall
b1df; mov si,di; pop di` -> SI=new, DI=parent, then initialise SI from DI.  Patches 258/270/457/298/281/
415/415 read `di` as the caller's object and folded the SI/DI split into "si==di": the port registered the
PARENT twice, zeroed the PARENT's body, orphaned the fresh slot, and wrote each child's init into its
parent.  Patch 429 (7745) already expected b1df to return the projectile -> it got the display index and
built the shell at DGROUP:<small int>.

Rebuilt 1:1 (each asm-verified, cited in the per-function comments): b1d6 (guarded fall-through into b1df,
was dead after b21d), b1df (returns DI; AX published as g_fist_b1df_ax), b294 (real SOURCE->NEW rep movsb
clone), 9caa/9cfd (type-0x11/0x18 children placed at the parent), ba33/ba49/ba5d (template spawn: child
gets the parent's position, ba49's velocity goes to the child), 9d7a (9db1 gets si=parent, di=new), a93e
(b10c wreck<-X, 60f9 replaces X by the wreck; 60f9 is a WORD table at stride 2), bc46 (ace0 gets ax=b1df's
AX, bx=target, si=new, di=firer; tail writes to SI), a46e/b355 (9caa takes the NEAR offset, not the
re-pointed host ptr), ace0 (projectile LAUNCH init, whole body), addb tail (a192 ax=bearing, cx=0578's
pitch, dx/cx outputs), 0578 (077e cx=0927's DX; pitch published as g_fist_0578_bx), a265 tail ([di+0x38]=
pitch, [di+0x99]=(range hi<<8)|LUT>>8), the weapon wrappers b6c9/b6e3/b725/b73b/b751/b767/b77d/b793
(si=new proj, di=firer; b6c9's random spread), 03a9 (2-axis rotation trig, DX output g_fist_03a9_dx) and
its ac?? consumer.  Shim: three published-register globals (tools/native_main.c).
